WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.862
Step three runs the inventory
against the fictional tenant.

2
00:00:03.862 --> 00:00:08.683
You give it the fixture, an output folder,
three Azure scopes, two subscriptions and

3
00:00:08.683 --> 00:00:13.575
the root management group, the exceptions
list, and the control-plane subscription.

4
00:00:13.575 --> 00:00:15.425
It reads thirty rows.

5
00:00:15.425 --> 00:00:19.875
In Azure, four are Tier 0,
five Tier 1 and one Tier 2.

6
00:00:19.875 --> 00:00:25.393
In Entra, eight are Tier 0, two Tier 1,
two Tier 2, and one is unclassified:

7
00:00:25.393 --> 00:00:30.813
a role that isn't in the tier file,
reported rather than assumed safe.

8
00:00:30.813 --> 00:00:35.575
The run raises ten findings, seven
warnings and one information item.

9
00:00:35.575 --> 00:00:38.276
And it writes everything
to the output folder,

10
00:00:38.276 --> 00:00:42.611
with a manifest that lists every request
it sent and the hash of every file

11
00:00:42.611 --> 00:00:46.875
it wrote, so a reviewer can check later
which calls produced the evidence.

12
00:00:46.875 --> 00:00:49.780
The scope list on the
slide is wrapped to fit.
